hello everyone welcome to our course on  blockchains and cryptocurrencies my name  is dan bunnet i'm a co-director of the  stanford center for blockchain research  and a professor of computer science here  at stanford i'm co-teaching this course  along with my colleague professor joe  grunfest thank you dan hello everyone my  name is joe grundfest i'm a former  commissioner of the united states  securities exchange commission but i'm  better now thanks for asking i'm also a  professor of law and business here at  stanford this course is a special  collaboration between the computer  science department at stanford and  stanford's law school our goal is to  look at blockchain technology through a  variety of lenses including those of  developers investors regulators and the  media along with your instructors you'll  hear from rising stars in this space  including juan binet founder of filecoin  and ceo protocol labs as well as fred  ursum and matt wong of paradigm fred's a  co-founder of coinbase and matt's a  former partner at sequoia capital  together they offer absolutely  tremendous insight that you simply can't  get anywhere else  by the end of this course you should  understand how blockchain technologies  and cryptocurrencies work what the  immediate and long-term opportunities  are as well as their challenges we want  to arm you with enough information to  decide for yourself how the technology  will evolve and what its impact will be  we hope you enjoy the course and we very  much look forward to speaking to you  soon thank you very much thanks everyone  and we hope you enjoy the course
 

